From: sie-mcp web <web@sie-mcp.local>
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] wasm: account icount2 per TB inside the TCI
 interpreter (TB header op)

With patch 0002 skipping the per-guest-insn icount2 helper on
emscripten (a libffi/JS roundtrip per instruction), something must
credit the icount2 clock per executed TB - including TBs reached via
goto_tb/goto_ptr chaining, which execute entirely inside one
tcg_qemu_tb_exec() call and never pass through cpu_tb_exec again.

- tcg/tci: tcg_out_tb_start() emits an INDEX_op_tci_tbhdr header op
  (opcode appended after tci_qemu_st_rrr, numbering-compatible with the
  0005 wasm32 DRAFT) carrying the TB's guest-insn count in its 20-bit
  immediate.
- tcg/tci.c: the header runs at EVERY TB entry - cpu_tb_exec call,
  goto_tb chain target, goto_ptr target - and advances the icount2
  clock (icount2_advance) + diagnostics (wasm_tb_account) by the TB's
  icount.  The clock stays strictly instruction-proportional while
  chained; interrupt checks are unaffected (gen_tb_start's icount_decr
  brcond runs at each TB start, chained or not).

Device-visible clock semantics change by at most one TB (typically a
few guest insns): an MMIO access mid-TB now sees a clock that already
includes the whole TB instead of the exact io-insn boundary.  Boot
verified: the S75 fullflash reaches the idle screen (wallpaper, clock,
"Поиск сети") with no >>EXIT<<, LCD updating.

Measured (S75 fullflash, headless Chromium, tools/serialwatch.mjs,
10 s WATCH samples; baseline = two runs of the pre-chaining build,
both within ±2% of each other):

  insns executed at fixed wall time   gain
  t=20 s    93M           -> 197M    +113%
  t=40 s    195M          -> 374M     +92%
  t=60 s    315M          -> 629M    +100%
  t=80 s    425M          -> 783M     +84%

  virtual time at t=60 s: 3.96 s -> 7.21 s (+82%)

Known accepted deviations (rare paths, measured harmless on the boot):
- goto_ptr-chained TBs (indirect branches) used to be uncounted; they
  are counted now (more accurate than before).
- the rom_device cpu_io_recompile rewind re-executes insns that the
  header already credited (over-counts the rewound prefix; flash
  commands are rare).

Wasm/fork-only (icount2).  Conflicts with the 0005 wasm32 DRAFT
(goto_tb/tci emitters); that patch needs a rebase onto this per-TB
header model.
---
diff --git a/tcg/tci.c b/tcg/tci.c
index 03b9294935..16737166bb 100644
--- a/tcg/tci.c
+++ b/tcg/tci.c
@@ -1183,6 +1183,26 @@ uintptr_t QEMU_DISABLE_CFI tcg_qemu_tb_exec(CPUArchState *env,
             }
             break;
 
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+        case INDEX_op_tci_tbhdr:
+            /*
+             * TB header (emitted by tcg_out_tb_start): advance the
+             * icount2 clock by this TB's guest-insn count.  Executed at
+             * every TB entry, including goto_tb/goto_ptr chain targets,
+             * so TB chaining (see tcg_out_goto_tb) keeps the clock
+             * instruction-proportional.  cpu_tb_exec() no longer
+             * accounts executed TBs.
+             */
+            tci_args_ri(insn, &r0, &t1);
+            {
+                extern void wasm_tb_account(unsigned insns);
+                extern void icount2_advance(uint32_t cycles);
+                wasm_tb_account((unsigned)t1);
+                icount2_advance((uint32_t)t1);
+            }
+            break;
+#endif
+
         case INDEX_op_br:
             tci_args_l(insn, tb_ptr, &ptr);
             tb_ptr = ptr;
diff --git a/tcg/tci/tcg-target-opc.h.inc b/tcg/tci/tcg-target-opc.h.inc
index f8bfffc125..a8ec938955 100644
--- a/tcg/tci/tcg-target-opc.h.inc
+++ b/tcg/tci/tcg-target-opc.h.inc
@@ -15,3 +15,9 @@ DEF(tci_setcond32, 1, 2, 1, TCG_OPF_NOT_PRESENT)
 DEF(tci_movcond32, 1, 2, 1, TCG_OPF_NOT_PRESENT)
 DEF(tci_qemu_ld_rrr, 1, 2, 0, TCG_OPF_NOT_PRESENT)
 DEF(tci_qemu_st_rrr, 0, 3, 0, TCG_OPF_NOT_PRESENT)
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+/* wasm only: TB header carrying the guest-insn count, executed at every
+ * TB entry (cpu_tb_exec call, goto_tb chain jump, goto_ptr target) so the
+ * icount2 clock advances per executed TB even while TBs are chained. */
+DEF(tci_tbhdr, 0, 0, 1, TCG_OPF_NOT_PRESENT)
+#endif
diff --git a/tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc b/tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc
index 1b22c70616..26c409648c 100644
--- a/tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc
+++ b/tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc
@@ -1238,7 +1238,15 @@ static inline void tcg_target_qemu_prologue(TCGContext *s)
 
 static void tcg_out_tb_start(TCGContext *s)
 {
-    /* nothing to do */
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    /*
+     * Emit the TB header (see INDEX_op_tci_tbhdr): the interpreter
+     * executes it at every TB entry and advances the icount2 clock by
+     * the TB's guest-insn count there.  This keeps the clock strictly
+     * instruction-proportional even when TBs are chained via goto_tb.
+     */
+    tcg_out_op_ri(s, INDEX_op_tci_tbhdr, 0, s->gen_tb->icount);
+#endif
 }
 
 bool tcg_target_has_memory_bswap(MemOp memop)
